    "title": "46th Olympiad: Two Tight Races Entering Final Weekend - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By JJ Lang ,\n1 days ago Team USA’s shot at gold took a significant hit in the Open after today’s 2½–1½ loss against hosts Uzbekistan in Round 9. The women’s team rebounded with a 3–1 victory over Canada. With 13/18 scores, both teams are tied for 11th entering the weekend’s final two rounds. By winning out, podium finishes remain possible for both teams, provided other matches break favorably. Read full article",
